Revision history for Milter-Recipe

1.001 2026-09-22 TEODESIAN
    - Add yamilter-corpus, Milter::Corpus and Milter::Corpus::Replay, to replay a pile of mail through recipes and report on the verdicts
    - Add Milter::Harness, to start and stop yamilter for tests
    - Milter::Client sends one SMFIC_HEADER per header (#1), sends the body raw and in chunks (#2), can report timeouts and EOF (#3), and returns modifications
    - Milter::Recipe accumulates header values, not only names (#4)
    - Milter::Recipe::config gives each recipe its own section, rather than whichever recipe asked first (#5)
    - yamilter no longer buffers its log output
    - Require perl 5.014, and meet the Troglodyne perlcritic policy
    - README.md is now generated from the Milter::Recipe POD
    - Milter::Recipe::EnvelopeMatch works (#6), and works with no_accum
    - Add Milter::Recipe->config_reply; recipes configured with action=discard no longer die looking for a reply code
    - Add Milter::Recipe::MailingList: refuse malformed RFC 2369, 2919 and 8058 list headers, list mail missing required ones, and unsubscribe links without a List-Unsubscribe header; accept trusted lists outright on your MX's DKIM (or optionally SPF) result
    - Add service.order, to set the order recipes run in
    - Recipes' end of message callbacks now run; the default accept used to run first and pre-empt them
    - The accumulated header and body start afresh for each message on a connection
    - Recipe configuration includes no_accum, as documented

1.000 2026-06-29 TEODESIAN
    - First release to CPAN
